course: dictionary
lesson: 155
title: African and capital letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Africa is a continent, one of the biggest pieces of land on Earth. The word «African» describes things from, of or about Africa. Because it comes from a place name, it always starts with a capital letter.
explain: «African» can work in three ways. It describes a thing, as in «African elephant». It names a person, as in «an African», meaning someone from Africa or whose family comes from there. It also appears in the names of plants and animals that live in Africa.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is in use. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or is it naming a person? In «An African elephant's two huge ears», it describes an elephant. The clues around the word tell you its job in the sentence.
fact: Africa is the second-largest continent in the world.
fact: Africa has more than fifty countries and many hundreds of languages.
fact: «African» always starts with a capital A, because it comes from a place name.
fact: An African elephant has two finger-like tips on its trunk, while an Asian elephant has one.
fact: In 1822 a stork in Germany was found with an African spear in its neck, which helped show that storks spend the winter in Africa.
exercise: «Lions hunt mostly from dusk to dawn on African grassland.» What does African tell us about the grassland? | It is very wet and muddy | It is in a jungle in India | *It is in Africa | It is made of sand
exercise: «Maya is an African, and her family moved to London.» What does «an African» mean here? | A type of cloud | A tall tree | *A person from Africa, or whose family comes from Africa | A school subject
exercise: Which animal name in the lessons includes the word African? | American porcupine | Gir lion | *African elephant | Asian elephant
test: «The African wild dog hunts in packs across the savanna.» Why does African start with a capital letter? | *Because it comes from Africa, a place name | Because it is the name of a school subject | Because it is the first word of a sentence | Because it is a very long word
test: «The African grey parrot can copy human voices.» What does African show about the parrot? | A colour | How big the parrot is | *Where the parrot lives or comes from | How old the parrot is
exam: Which sentence uses African as a noun? | Lions rest for up to 20 hours a day. | The African elephant flaps its ears to cool down. | The savanna is an African grassland. | *Their neighbour is an African, from Kenya.
